  "id": "seated-machine-back-extension",
  "name": "Seated Machine Back Extension",
  "definition": "A supported compound seated back extension on the exact Life Fitness Insignia SS-BE selectorized fixture. The hips remain seated against the lumbar pad and the feet rest on the foot support while the torso presses the posterior roller backward, finishing when the lower back contacts the lumbar pad. Spinal extension and hip extension are a disclosed categorical inference from the manufacturer execution, extensor/gluteal context, and schematic hip opening; the diagrams do not partition lumbar versus pelvic excursion or establish numeric joint ranges. Lumbar extensors are primary and gluteus maximus secondary by back-extension emphasis and existing action capabilities. This is not fully restrained MedX lumbar isolation, a hip-only Roman-chair extension, an unsupported hinge, a reverse hyper, or another machine model. Lumbar extensors receive truthful region credit without a substitute body-model surface.",
  "evidenceRefs": [
    "life-fitness-2024-insignia-series-manual",
    "christophy-2012-lumbar-spine",
    "arnold-2010-lower-limb"
  ],
